A||||6||Leadfoot||Spark plug boots are arcing||||1||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||11-12-2001||03:54 PM||||Last night I moved my car to a new storage spot.  As it was running I opened the truck to make sure nothing was in it.  I forgot I took the trunk light out when I was fixing the engine blower motor so it was pitch black back there.  However, looking down at the engine all I saw was blue sparks coming from each of the metal shields that go over the spark plug boots.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> I just replaced the wires with the so called performance brand.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> Do any of you know of a good set of spark plug wires that won't give me these arcing woes?   <p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||samoht||11-12-2001||05:13 PM||||How are the plugs, .45 gap , clean ?  Good engine ground?  Just some thoughts||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||11-12-2001||06:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by samoht:<BR><B>How are the plugs, .45 gap , clean ?  Good engine ground?  Just some thoughts</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>New plugs were installed with a 0.45 gap 3000 miles ago.  The engine ground is good.  I just wire brushed the stud to which is attached to when I installed the 1.6 rockers.  Just to clarify I have a stock coil.  I am wondering if the steel boot covers are needed.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||California Kid||11-12-2001||06:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leadfoot:<BR><B> I am wondering if the steel boot covers are needed.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Seems to me that they were there for a reason! Put them on and check it out.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||avengador1||11-12-2001||09:07 PM||||The steel boot covers are heat shields. Mine were arching till I replaced the spark plug wires. I got a bosch set this time till I get an MSD set of 8 or 8.5 mm. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||11-12-2001||10:13 PM||||Pep Boys, Barrington Road, 5th or 6th aisle bottom right shelf. Accel 8.8mm Wires. Get the straight boots. They are cut to fit for a V-8 so you'll have some left-over wires.<BR>Work wonders. No arcs and can be used with upgraded ignition systems.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000006||Leadfoot||11-13-2001||09:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by California Kid:<BR><B> [QUOTE]Originally posted by Leadfoot:<BR>[b] I am wondering if the steel boot covers are needed.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Seems to me that they were there for a reason! Put them on and check it out.<P>[/B][/QUOTE]<P>I do have the boots on and that's why they are arcing.<P>Oreif thanks! I'll pick them up today before work.<BR>||||reg||1
